.TH WB\-ACCEPT 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-accept \- accept the file of an issue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR accept <issue> [\-\-no\-commit]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Accept the issue's file .watchbill/issues/<issue>.yml: read it, hold it to its form, refuse it while it holds a question, say what will be written, and write .watchbill/issues/<issue>.accepted with the SHA\-256 of the file, the git user.name and user.email, and the time in UTC. An acceptance that is there is never written over.
.PP
Then it commits the acceptance alone, on the issue's branch, with nothing else. It refuses first when the checkout is not on that branch or the issue's file is not committed as it is.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-commit
Only write the acceptance and say the commit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It is accepted.
.TP
.B 1
It is refused: no file, a fault of form, a question, an acceptance that is there, no git identity, a path of changes under build_files, or a list that leaves out what a file needs to build.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly (no issue, a word that is not known, a name that is not an issue), the folder is not in a git repository, or Watchbill is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
